.\" Manpage for webpage2pdf.
.TH WEBPAGE2PDF 1 "2026-09-07" "webpage2pdf 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
webpage2pdf \- turn web pages into clean A4 PDFs that read like typeset essays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webpage2pdf
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fISOURCE\fR...
.br
.B w2p
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fISOURCE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B webpage2pdf
works out which part of a web page is actually the article, discards the rest,
and re\-typesets the content for paper.
.PP
Saving a page from a browser keeps the site's screen layout and hands pagination
to an engine that treats page\-break rules as optional, which is why you get
sidebars, cookie banners, and images sliced across two pages. This tool rebuilds
the document instead: it scores every container for prose density, strips the
furniture, normalises the heading hierarchy, caps image heights so no figure can
exceed one page, and renders through WeasyPrint, which enforces
.B break-inside: avoid
rather than treating it as a hint.
.PP
Each \fISOURCE\fR is an http(s) URL or a path to a saved
.I .html
file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write to this exact path. Accepts a single source only; use
.B \-\-dir
for batches.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Output directory. Filenames are derived from article titles, with
.IR name \-2.pdf ", " name \-3.pdf
used when a name is taken.
.TP
.BR \-\-from\-list " \fIFILE\fR"
Read sources from a text file, one per line. Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile " \fINAME\fR"
A named bundle of settings:
.BR essay " (default), " reference ", " booklet ", " device ", " screen ", "
.BR ereader ", " notes .
A profile fixes the format, the page geometry, the link handling and the
numbering together, because those are not independent choices \(em footnotes
suit paper and are pointless on screen. Any other flag you give overrides it.
Add your own as TOML under
.IR ~/.config/webpage2pdf/profiles/ ;
one sharing a built\-in name replaces it. See
.BR \-\-list\-profiles .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIFMT\fR"
Output format:
.BR pdf " (default), " html ", " epub ", " md .
When not given it is taken from the output filename, so
.B \-o piece.epub
is enough.
.B html
is a single self\-contained file with fonts and images embedded and subset to
the characters used;
.B epub
reflows, which is the right shape for a phone or an e\-reader;
.B md
carries YAML front matter and writes images to a sidecar folder.
.TP
.BR \-\-preset " \fINAME\fR"
Page geometry:
.BR a4 " (default), " letter ", " a5 ", " book ", " remarkable ", " two-column .
A preset drives both the stylesheet and the image fitting from one set of
numbers, so an image that fits a single page on A4 also fits one on A5.
.B book
mirrors its inner and outer margins across facing pages, for double-sided
printing or binding. See
.BR \-\-list\-presets .
.TP
.BR \-\-toc ", " \-\-no\-toc
Force or suppress the contents list. By default one appears when the document
has at least four top-level sections and 1500 words. Page numbers are resolved
by the layout engine, so they stay correct however long the list itself is.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open each finished PDF in the default viewer.
.TP
.BR \-\-style " \fINAME\fR"
Stylesheet to typeset with. See
.BR \-\-list\-styles .
Default:
.BR essay .
.TP
.BR \-\-links " \fIplain\fR|\fIendnotes\fR|\fIfootnotes\fR|\fIkeep\fR"
How to treat hyperlinks.
.B plain
strips link styling and is cleanest on paper;
.B endnotes
adds superscript markers and a numbered list at the end;
.B footnotes
sets each URL at the foot of the page it appears on, which is easier to read
than an endnote because the reference is already in view;
.B keep
leaves links live. Default:
.BR plain .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-numbering
Omit the automatic section and figure numbers.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-images
Text only. Much smaller files, and faster.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-url ", " \-\-no\-standfirst
Trim the title block: drop the source URL, or the italic summary line.
.TP
.BR \-\-keep\-html " \fIFILE\fR"
Also write the cleaned HTML. Useful for seeing exactly what was removed.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " \fIN\fR"
Fetch this many pages at once when converting a batch. Default 4. Only fetching
is parallel; rendering stays on one thread, because WeasyPrint offers no
thread\-safety guarantee and drives Pango through cffi with shared fontconfig
state. The network is the part that takes the time.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Neither read from nor write to the fetch cache.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Re\-fetch even when a cached copy is held. Use after a page has been updated.
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-info
Report what the cache holds, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-cache
Delete everything in the cache, and exit. Nothing there is precious.
.TP
.B \-\-fix
With
.BR \-\-doctor ,
attempt the repairs it recommends rather than only printing them. Every command
is shown before it runs.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " \fISEC\fR"
Network timeout per request. Default: 30.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-styles
Print available stylesheet names and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-presets
Print available page presets and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-profiles
Print available profiles and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Check the interpreter, native libraries and every Python package, then report
the exact fix for anything missing. Works even when the PDF engine cannot load.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print errors only.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH PIPELINES
.B \-
as a source reads HTML from standard input, and
.B \-o \-
writes the finished file to standard output. Progress is written to standard
error, so it cannot corrupt the document.
.PP
.RS
.nf
pbpaste | w2p \- \-o \- > clipping.pdf
curl \-s https://example.com/essay | w2p \- \-o \- \-f md >> log.md
cat urls.txt | w2p \-\-from\-list \- \-d reading/
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Convert a single essay:
.B webpage2pdf https://example.com/some\-essay
.TP
A saved file, to a chosen path:
.B w2p saved\-page.html \-o reading/week\-03.pdf
.TP
A batch, named from article titles:
.B w2p url1 url2 saved.html \-d reading/
.TP
A week's reading list, with links collected as endnotes:
.B w2p \-\-from\-list links.txt \-d reading/ \-\-links endnotes
.SH TYPOGRAPHY
Output is A4 by default \(em see
.B \-\-preset
for other geometries \(em set in Literata, bundled with the tool so that the
same page produces the same document on every machine. Old\-style figures in
running text, lining tabular figures in tables, justified with hyphenation, and
first\-line indents. The hyphenation dictionary is chosen from the source page's
declared language, so non\-English articles break on the right morpheme
boundaries. Figures are atomic: an image is scaled to fit within a single page
before rendering, and cannot be split from its caption.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/webpage2pdf/config.toml
Defaults you would otherwise retype:
.BR profile ", " dir ", " jobs ", " timeout ", " open ", " cache .
Command\-line flags override it.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Caches/webpage2pdf
Fetched pages and images. Pages are held for a day, images for a month.
.TP
.I ~/.config/webpage2pdf/profiles/*.toml
User\-defined profiles.
.TP
.I styles/essay.css
The stylesheet. Copy it to
.I styles/<name>.css
and it becomes available as
.BR "\-\-style <name>" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All sources converted.
.TP
.B 1
At least one source failed, or the arguments were invalid.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR webpage2pdf-server (1)
for the local drag\-and\-drop web front end.
.SH BUGS
JavaScript\-rendered and paywalled pages yield little text, because the HTML the
server sends is what gets parsed; no scripts are run. Save such a page from your
browser and convert the file. The tool warns when a result looks suspiciously
thin.
